    "created_at": "2016-07-21T04:57:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-21T04:57:44Z",
    "body": "I don't think it's possible for appending the child to fail. If it failed by throwing an exception in some way (perhaps custom elements could make this happen?), we would just rethrow that exception; that's generally implied when one algorithm calls another.\n\nDo you have some example code of the situation you're thinking of?\n\n(Also, to be clear, if you try to assign something that is not a HTMLCaptionElement, it will throw, by the IDL. I'm not sure if that's what the first part of your sentence was getting at.)\n",
