    "created_at": "2016-07-21T05:28:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-21T05:28:53Z",
    "body": "Ah, wow, very interesting!\n\nI think this should rethrow the exception, yes. I'm not sure if we should try to make this clearer somehow... it seems like if we added some clarification here, we'd end up adding it for pretty much every place in the spec that uses \"append\". Maybe that's not a bad thing? Maybe there aren't actually that many places in HTML that allow appending elements? Searching through it's basically this and other places on HTMLTableElement.\n\nSo yeah, I guess it would be good to add \"rethrow any exceptions\" to the appends/inserts on the HTMLTableElement algorithms. We can definitely revise the spec to do that.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
